## Continuous Integration and Releases

Pushes to the principal branch and scheduled runs perform builds and retain
their artifacts; neither event publishes a release. A successful manual
workflow dispatch publishes a release after the packaging job completes.
The person initiating that dispatch must select one of four channels:
`alpha`, `beta`, `rc`, or `stable`. Alpha, beta, and rc releases are marked
as pre-releases; stable releases are not.
